---
globs: *.ts,*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

## Common

- don't forget to apply @.editorconfig
- Force absolute imports (from common root configured as @)
- Do not import as type whenever possible
- Do not use .cursorrules file - it is deprecated. Use .cursor/rules/\*.mdc files instead.
- No workarounds for backward compatibility - refactor straight away or report to user if necessary
- TypeScript class conventions:
- Always annotate field types explicitly
- Prefer plain parameters on functions over one-off `{ ... }` types whose only job is to bundle arguments; use object parameters when the shape is a real boundary (e.g. zod-parsed request body, public API) or there are enough fields that callsites become unreadable

## OOP

- constants, then public class fields, then private class fields, then constructor, then public methods, then private methods
- Access modifiers (public, private, protected) and readonly (where applicable) are mandatory, especially for constructor parameters that initialize class fields
- no static methods
- private static readonly variables (constants) are okay, use them for config as well, uppercase
- method return types are mandatory
- initialization of fields outside of constructor is preferable

## Naming Conventions

- No class names containing manager (e.g., UserManager, DataManager, Manager)
- Use more specific, descriptive names that reflect the class's actual responsibility (e.g., UserService, DataRepository, EventHandler)

## Comments

- Do not add new obvious comments that just restate what the code already clearly expresses
- Adding comments for unclear logic or heavy math is perfectly fine
- Do not remove existing comments
